<concept importance="optional" id="t00518">
	<title>Safe Exit Warning (SEW)</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>safe exit warning (SEW)</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03438">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03439">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_D10_002_E.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>While your vehicle is stopped, Safe Exit Warning may help you avoid a collision using a warning message and warning sound if it detects a vehicle approaching the rear corner of your vehicle and a passenger opens a door.</p>
		<note type="tip">
			<p>The timing of the warning may vary, depending on the speed of the approaching vehicle.</p>
		</note>
		<section>
			<title>Detection sensor</title>
			<p>Please refer to <xref href="t00444.dita#t00444"/> for the applicable sensors and their locations.</p>
			<note type="tip">
				<p>For more information about the rear corner radars, refer to <xref href="t00507.dita#t00507"/>.</p>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
